            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a homomorphism of meet-semilattices.
          %h3#filter_of_subsets Filter of subsets
          %p
            A
            %strong filter of subsets
            of a given set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a filter on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#as_proobjects As pro-objects
          %p
            Under the correspondence between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+sets"} upper sets
            and duals of (0,1)-copresheaves, filters correspond to duals of precisely those copresheaves that are cofiltered limits of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corepresentable"} corepresentables
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-objects"} pro-objects
            of posets, dual to how ideals can be viewed as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-objects"} ind-objects
          %h3#in_dependent_type_theory In dependent type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega, \mathrm{El}_\Omega)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            with its type reflector type family. Given a type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is given by the function type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to \Omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:T, U:T \to \Omega \vdash x \in F
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
